@startuml
title What each link in the chain actually proves
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFCFF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5

package "Public artefacts" {
  component "Git tag\n2026-07-31T0519-v5.6.0" as TAG
  component "Published DFU\ncoldcard.com/downloads" as DFU
  component "signatures.txt\nPGP-signed SHA-256 list" as SIGS
}

package "What you can run" {
  component "make repro\n(Docker, pinned Alpine)" as REPRO
  component "signit split / check" as SIGNIT
  component "hexdump diff" as DIFF
}

package "What the device checks" {
  component "Header signature\nsecp256k1, 6 trusted keys" as HDR
  component "World checksum\nin SE1 slot 14" as WC
  component "OTP high-water\ntimestamps" as OTP
  component "Bootloader self-hash\ncallgate method 1" as SELF
}

TAG --> REPRO : source under test
DFU --> SIGNIT : split into firmware + bootrom
REPRO --> DIFF
SIGNIT --> DIFF
SIGS --> DFU : integrity of the download

DIFF --> HDR : same bytes as published
HDR --> WC : what is running now
WC --> OTP
SELF -[#B54A4A]-> HDR : the one part repro cannot rebuild

note bottom of DIFF
  proves: the published binary
  came from this source tree
end note

note bottom of WC
  proves: nothing in flash changed
  since the owner last approved it
end note

note right of SELF
  the bootloader is factory-set and
  not rebuilt by make repro; it can only
  be hashed in place with a fresh nonce
end note
@enduml
